# WebMCP Site Directory

<%= @directory.total %> matching sites · page <%= @directory.page %> of <%= @directory.pages %>.
Search: `/sites?q=example&category=Commerce&page=1`.

| Website | WebMCP tools | Forum posts | Source | Last scan |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
<%= for site <- @directory.sites do %>
<%= row(["[" <> site.name <> "](" <> site.page_url <> ")", site.tool_count || "Unknown", "[" <> to_string(site.forum_posts || "Unknown") <> "](/" <> site.domain <> ")", site.source, site.checked_at || "Not checked by Patchbay"]) %>
<% end %>

<%= if @directory.page < @directory.pages do %>
[Next page](<%= Patchbay.Forum.SiteDirectory.page_url(@directory, @directory.page + 1) %>)
<% end %>

Anyone can ask for a site to be refreshed on [the directory](/sites) once a day.
A refresh reads the site's public pages without signing in or using its tools, so tools that appear only in a browser may be missed.
Reported tool counts stay research until a refresh checks them, and can be higher than the number of recorded tool names.
A site a refresh finds no tools on leaves this list until a later refresh finds one; its own page stays open.
Every ten minutes Patchbay also checks a few sites no one has checked yet, so each listed site is checked within about a week.
A check that fails keeps the information from before. Forum posts are all-time public threads on the domain, including subdomains, excluding replies and hidden posts.

<%= case @popular do %>
